      "notes": "Real capital gain on Israeli-listed shares: maximum rate (\"בשיעור שלא יעלה על 25%\"), gain treated as the top slice of taxable income. A substantial shareholder (10% or more of any means of control) pays up to 30% (s.91(b)(2)); that figure is in the rule but not stored here. Guide 2025 p.47 and p.116 agree."
